WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.100
-House Republicans have once
again descended into chaos

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.300
and paralyzed Congress

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.868
after they ousted
former speaker Kevin McCarthy,

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.634
who lasted just
nine months on the job,

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.534
replaced him with nobody,
and then left town.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.701
And now some Republicans
and GOP pundits

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:15.634
are floating the possibility
of making Donald Trump

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:16.834
the new Speaker of the House.

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:19.133
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.801
Here is where we're at
in America right now.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:28.200
Yesterday, a former president
of the United States

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.601
was placed under a gag order
by a judge.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.467
And it somehow wasn't even
the biggest news of the day.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.834
-Tonight the judge
in Donald Trump's fraud trial

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:38.767
is issuing a gag order
against the former president.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.300
It bans him
from speaking publicly

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.767
about members
of the court staff.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.133
-For the first time ever,

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.601
a former president
of the United States

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.701
was slapped with a gag order.

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:50.667
-Yes, this is the first time
a former president

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.033
has been slapped
with a gag order,

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.868
unless you count the time
Hillary told Bill

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:55.601
to shut up at a dinner party.

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.868
[ As Bill Clinton ] Did I ever
tell you guys about the time

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:59.334
I got drunk with Boris Yeltsin?

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:00.734
[ Normal voice ]
Yes. Yes, you did.

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:04.801
The last time was,
let's see now, five minutes ago.

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:06.067
Now, this gag order means

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.901
Trump can no longer talk
about court staff in public,

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.434
although it's very possible

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:12.767
Trump misunderstood
the meaning of the word "gag."

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.901
[ As Trump ] So now your dear --
your dear former president

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:19.734
can't do gags, can't do pranks,
can't do goofs of any time.

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:22.734
So -- So now if I tell you
to pull my finger,

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:24.634
I have to legally add,
when you do it,

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:25.934
I'm going to fart.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:33.300
And that's sad, because that
takes all the fun out of it.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.834
[ Normal voice ] That was not
the lead story yesterday,

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:36.234
because, of course,
this happened.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:39.334
-For the first time in the
history of American democracy

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:41.767
and the first Congress of 1789,

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:45.200
the Speaker of the House has
been removed from his position

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.767
as the leader of the chamber.

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.100
By a vote of 216 to 210,

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.901
lawmakers booted
Speaker Kevin McCarthy,

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.934
throwing the House into chaos

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.067
and into
unprecedented territory.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.734
-This is the first time
it's ever happened.

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:00.267
Republicans have a knack
for creating history

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.467
in the most embarrassing way.

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:03.234
It's like saying,
hey, the Jets made history.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.968
This is the first time
in his career

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.734
Aaron Rodgers has gone
a whole season

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.667
without throwing
an interception.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.067
And, yeah.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.167
Yeah, guys,
the Jets jokes are back.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:19.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.167
When it looked like they were
going to be good this year,

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:24.601
I was worried...

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:28.367
because we need Jets jokes.

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.167
But then Rodgers tore his ACL,

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.667
and as sad as it was
for Jets fans,

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.100
it was a relief
for comedy writers.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.133
Is it a coincidence that ACL

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:37.033
are also the initials
of "A Closer Look"?

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:38.200
I don't know.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.567
It's pretty [bleep] suspicious.

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:44.801
So House Republicans
are in chaos,

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:45.868
although I'm not sure

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.434
we can call this
unprecedented territory

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:49.200
since House Republicans
are always in chaos.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.300
We've been saying the
Republican Party is in chaos

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.801
on this show for eight years.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.934
We just use the same
cue card over and over.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:57.200
Wally keeps it on standby
at all times.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.834
Can I just say, Wally,

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.567
it is great to be back
at work with you.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.000
And I did check.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.834
You will still get paid extra
every time you have a line.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:12.234
And the moment the vote tally
was finished was also historic,

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:13.667
because as far
as anyone can tell,

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.934
it's the first time these words
have ever been uttered.

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:22.234
-On this vote, the yeas are 216.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.033
The nays are 210.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.100
The resolution is adopted.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:31.200
Without objection, the motion to
reconsider is laid on the table.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.167
The office
of Speaker of the House

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.934
of the United States
House of Representatives

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:40.067
is hereby declared vacant.
[ Gavel bangs ]

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.968
-Cool, so the position that's
third in line to the presidency

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:46.100
is currently like
a [bleep] roadside motel.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.367
Then they adjourned and left
town without picking someone.

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.767
Here's the moment
Congressman Patrick McHenry,

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.868
a McCarthy ally,
adjourned the session.

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:54.334
And you can tell how mad he is

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.200
because he really pounded
that thing.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.968
-The chair declares
the House in recess,

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:00.601
subject to the call
of the chair.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.400
[ Gavel bangs ]
-Whoa!

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:11.601
Was he closing the session

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:15.367
or trying to win a stuffed panda
at the county fair?

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:17.567
He went after that like
a Brooklyn third grader

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:20.234
killing a spotted lantern fly.

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:22.667
And look, I know they're
an invasive species

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.067
and killing them
is the right play.

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.334
But I think we've all seen
a kid doing it

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:28.868
with a little too much panache

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:33.133
who makes you think, "Oh, this
is just a starter kit for them."

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:34.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:39.334
So they fired the speaker,

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:41.000
then just left town
without picking a new one.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.801
It's very Republican Party
to take step one

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:44.767
without putting any thought
into step two.

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:46.300
"Well, I just sold
my apartment."

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.534
"Cool.
Where are you moving to?"

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.501
"Moving.

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:50.801
Can't I just stay here?"

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:52.901
"No, if you want to stay here,
why'd you sell it?"

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:55.234
"Well, I wanted the money."
"You can't have both."

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:57.300
"Uhh. Shh. Quiet.
I'm trying to think."

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.133
[ Snoring ]

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:01.133
"Did you just fall asleep
while you were thinking?"

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:04.968
"I don't know, man.
I'm so [bleep] tired."

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:06.634
Now, as historic
as this development is,

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:08.234
it's also not
all that surprising.

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:11.667
Kevin McCarthy has never exactly
been the most gifted politician.

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.367
He's not especially charismatic.

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:14.634
He doesn't seem
to stand for anything.

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:16.834
And sometimes
it's just genuinely hard

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:18.667
to understand
what he's trying to say,

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:22.400
like when he appeared at a Trump
rally in 2020 and said this.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.534
-I want you to watch
Nancy Pelosi hand me that gavel.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:27.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:30.734
And I promise you this.

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:32.534
I won't bang her with it,

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:36.901
but I'll bang the end to the
socialism and yes to America.

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.968
-It's hard to be onstage
with Trump

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:51.234
and be the one making
the least amount of sense.

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:54.501
"I'll bang the end of the
socialism and yes to America."

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:58.067
Why does he sound like a print
ad for Budweiser in Malaysia?

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.634
If someone you love ever starts
talking like that,

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:06.334
you need to immediately
call 911,

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:09.000
or as Kevin would say,
"Call one, then another one,

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.200
and then before
both of those, a nine."

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.167
So McCarthy wasn't an especially
memorable political talent,

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.200
and he had to endure
all kinds of indignities

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.934
to climb his way
to the top of the garbage heap

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:21.367
that is
the House Republican caucus,

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:23.734
like the time Donald Trump
just called him

00:06:23.734 --> 00:06:26.801
by a completely different name
and McCarthy didn't correct him.

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:29.667
-There was progress today.
I look forward to solving it.

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:30.868
-Thank you, Steve.

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:32.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:34.567
-"Thank you, Steve."
"My name is Kevin."

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:36.968
"It's Steve now.

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:41.000
Go change your birth certificate
or get lost."

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.234
Now, in Trump's defense,

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:45.067
he was about to introduce
someone named Steve,

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:47.200
but because his brain
is just ooze,

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.167
he misfired
and called McCarthy Steve.

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:50.801
I think part of the reason
is that whenever Trump

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:53.100
has to read something off a
teleprompter at a formal event,

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:56.033
as opposed to just vomiting up
off-the-cuff babble

00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:57.400
about toilets and windmills,

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.801
he has to get the gears
in motion way in advance.

00:06:59.801 --> 00:07:01.934
The whole time Kevin McCarthy
was speaking,

00:07:01.934 --> 00:07:04.300
I'm sure Trump was standing
behind him thinking

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.234
[As Trump] Okay, Steve is next.
Steve, Steve, Steve.

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:09.968
Wait. Who the hell is this guy?
Screw it. Just go with Steve."

00:07:09.968 --> 00:07:12.667
Everybody's Steve now.
Everybody's Steve.

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:14.200
And that's a flub.
That's not a gag.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.601
So it's legally allowed.

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:18.901
It doesn't violate the order.

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:20.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:23.701
Never mind.

00:07:23.701 --> 00:07:25.100
[ Normal voice ]
But that's the modern GOP.

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.534
You have to endure
endless humiliation

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:27.968
just to get a job that sucks.

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:29.367
And that wasn't the last

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:31.200
of the many indignities
McCarthy suffered.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.501
In order to curry favor

00:07:32.501 --> 00:07:34.601
with the hard-liners
in his caucus,

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:35.801
he had to fly down to Mar-a-Lago

00:07:35.801 --> 00:07:37.300
for that infamous picture
with Donald Trump

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.501
just three weeks after
the insurrection on January 6th.

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:41.934
He had to smile for a photo
with the guy

00:07:41.934 --> 00:07:43.400
who tried to overturn
American democracy

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.267
and might have
almost got him killed.

00:07:45.267 --> 00:07:46.801
It's like watching the Alien
and the Predator

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:50.534
team up for a podcast
called "No Hard Feelings."

00:07:50.534 --> 00:07:52.267
McCarthy also attempted
to portray himself

00:07:52.267 --> 00:07:54.501
as a serious statesman prepared
for the job of speaker.

00:07:54.501 --> 00:07:56.334
But his attempts were not
especially impressive,

00:07:56.334 --> 00:07:59.834
like when he unveiled
what he said would be his agenda

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:02.367
if he became speaker,
but it was comically thin.

00:08:02.367 --> 00:08:05.501
-What we're gonna roll out today
is a commitment to America,

00:08:05.501 --> 00:08:07.434
and we want to roll it out
to you,

00:08:07.434 --> 00:08:12.367
to the entire country,
to know exactly what we will do

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:15.667
if you would trust us
and give us the ability

00:08:15.667 --> 00:08:17.968
to take a new direction
for this country.

00:08:17.968 --> 00:08:20.767
What the commitment is,
is a plan,

00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:22.701
a plan for a new direction.

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:25.167
So you know what?

00:08:25.167 --> 00:08:27.868
We've created
a commitment to America.

00:08:27.868 --> 00:08:29.300
-That's your plan?
It's one page.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.334
It looks like a leaflet
they hand out in Times Square

00:08:31.334 --> 00:08:34.167
for 15% off
at Bubba Gump Shrimp.

00:08:34.167 --> 00:08:36.167
If you buy deodorant
and gum at CVS,

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:39.100
you get a receipt
that's way longer than that.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.734
But that tells you
why McCarthy failed

00:08:40.734 --> 00:08:42.767
and why so many Republican
speakers before him have failed,

00:08:42.767 --> 00:08:44.234
from John Boehner to Paul Ryan.

00:08:44.234 --> 00:08:46.934
Republicans don't actually have
a discernible ideological agenda

00:08:46.934 --> 00:08:47.968
that they all agree on.

00:08:47.968 --> 00:08:49.934
There are no coherent
policy goals

00:08:49.934 --> 00:08:51.567
other than cutting taxes
for rich people

00:08:51.567 --> 00:08:53.767
and banning woke
antifa Barbie dolls.

00:08:53.767 --> 00:08:55.834
And none of those things
are popular with voters.

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:58.367
So they end up
in this nonstop vicious cycle

00:08:58.367 --> 00:08:59.901
where a speaker gets elected,

00:08:59.901 --> 00:09:02.501
a bunch of hard-liners
demand that he do crazy [bleep]

00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:04.634
he says no,
then they take him out back

00:09:04.634 --> 00:09:06.300
and hit him over
the head like this.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.234
[ Gavel bangs ]

00:09:07.234 --> 00:09:09.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:15.367
So it all ended in humiliation
for McCarthy and his allies,

00:09:15.367 --> 00:09:16.834
which is fitting,
because McCarthy

00:09:16.834 --> 00:09:19.567
had to humiliate himself to get
the job in the first place.

00:09:19.567 --> 00:09:21.834
He basically had to crawl
over broken glass

00:09:21.834 --> 00:09:23.167
to get hired for a [bleep] job

00:09:23.167 --> 00:09:24.434
he couldn't even keep
for nine months.

00:09:24.434 --> 00:09:25.801
Remember, back in January,

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:27.267
when he lost the vote
for speaker

00:09:27.267 --> 00:09:29.634
over and over and over again

00:09:29.634 --> 00:09:32.133
and he just had to
sit there in shame

00:09:32.133 --> 00:09:35.067
while the clerk announced
that no speaker had been elected

00:09:35.067 --> 00:09:36.934
14 times in a row

00:09:36.934 --> 00:09:40.167
like he was living in some sort
of David Lynchian nightmare.

00:09:40.167 --> 00:09:42.567
-A speaker has not been elected.

00:09:42.567 --> 00:09:44.634
A speaker has not been elected.

00:09:44.701 --> 00:09:46.701
A speaker has not been elected.

00:09:46.701 --> 00:09:48.767
A speaker has not...
A speaker has not...

00:09:48.767 --> 00:09:49.901
A speaker has not...
Has not...

00:09:49.901 --> 00:09:51.033
Has not...
Has not...

00:09:51.033 --> 00:09:53.334
Not... Not... Not...
Not... Not been elected.

00:09:53.334 --> 00:09:55.901
-It is happening again.

00:09:55.901 --> 00:09:57.634
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.634 --> 00:09:59.834
-McCarthy finally got the job
on the 15th try

00:09:59.834 --> 00:10:01.234
after making a bunch
of promises,

00:10:01.234 --> 00:10:04.067
like, for example,
implementing a new rule

00:10:04.067 --> 00:10:05.968
that any one member
of the GOP caucus

00:10:05.968 --> 00:10:07.400
could bring a motion
to remove him,

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.334
which is exactly
what they did to him.

00:10:09.334 --> 00:10:11.434
And even knowing that,
he still dared his critics,

00:10:11.434 --> 00:10:13.133
specifically Florida
congressman Matt Gaetz,

00:10:13.133 --> 00:10:15.200
to try to get rid of him
before the vote was called.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:18.567
-If somebody wants to make
a motion against me, bring it.

00:10:18.567 --> 00:10:19.667
-[ As McCarthy ]
That's right. Bring it.

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:21.467
And I can promise you this.

00:10:21.467 --> 00:10:23.334
If you call a vote to remove me,

00:10:23.334 --> 00:10:26.067
I'll take that gavel
and I won't bang you with it,

00:10:26.067 --> 00:10:29.567
but I will gavel it
to make a banging sound

00:10:29.567 --> 00:10:32.133
that gavels the end
to yes America.

00:10:32.133 --> 00:10:34.067
Oh [bleep]
I'm going to get replaced.

00:10:34.067 --> 00:10:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.701 --> 00:10:38.267
[ Normal voice ]
Well, Gaetz and his small band

00:10:38.267 --> 00:10:40.767
of kooks and weirdos did bring
it, and McCarthy is now gone.

00:10:40.767 --> 00:10:42.133
And because
you have to be insane

00:10:42.133 --> 00:10:43.434
to actually want this job,

00:10:43.434 --> 00:10:45.367
some Republicans are floating
the name of a person

00:10:45.367 --> 00:10:47.267
who is, in fact, insane.

00:10:47.267 --> 00:10:49.133
-Sources telling me at this hour

00:10:49.133 --> 00:10:52.467
some House Republicans
have been in contact with

00:10:52.467 --> 00:10:54.033
and have started an effort

00:10:54.033 --> 00:10:56.434
to draft former president
Donald Trump

00:10:56.434 --> 00:10:58.033
to be the next speaker.

00:10:58.033 --> 00:11:01.901
And I have been told
that President Trump

00:11:01.901 --> 00:11:04.534
might be open to helping
the Republican Party,

00:11:04.534 --> 00:11:07.167
at least in the short term,
if necessary.

00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:08.667
-Incredible.
Only the Republicans

00:11:08.667 --> 00:11:11.133
would consider
giving the job of speaker

00:11:11.133 --> 00:11:13.567
to someone who is
under a gag order.

00:11:13.567 --> 00:11:15.334
[ Laughter ]

00:11:15.334 --> 00:11:17.501
It's like hiring a French mime

00:11:17.501 --> 00:11:20.567
as your new NFL
play-by-play guy.

00:11:20.567 --> 00:11:21.701
Marcel, what do you think

00:11:21.701 --> 00:11:24.167
of this play the Chiefs
are drawing up?

00:11:24.167 --> 00:11:26.567
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.567 --> 00:11:29.100
I agree, Marcel.
Ravens defense is like a wall.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.000
What's that?
You have something else to add?

00:11:33.167 --> 00:11:37.100
Oh, you also want to talk
about Taylor Swift?

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:40.467
I'm with you, Marcel.
I can't get enough of it.

00:11:40.467 --> 00:11:41.901
Also, I like when Hannity,

00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:44.133
who is best friends with Trump
and talks to him constantly,

00:11:44.133 --> 00:11:46.667
says sources are telling him
Trump is open to it.

00:11:46.667 --> 00:11:48.567
So Trump told you that?

00:11:48.567 --> 00:11:50.968
"Sources" is just
Trump's Mafia nickname.

00:11:50.968 --> 00:11:51.968
"Where'd I hear that?

00:11:51.968 --> 00:11:54.701
Oh, I got it from
Donny Sources."

00:11:54.701 --> 00:11:57.834
[ Laughter ]

00:11:57.834 --> 00:12:00.100
But this perfectly sums up
the current state

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.100
of the Republican Party.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:02.834
Usually when someone's in court,

00:12:02.834 --> 00:12:04.734
they have to call a friend
to ask for help.

00:12:04.734 --> 00:12:08.234
In this case, he's calling
from court to offer it.

00:12:08.234 --> 00:12:10.167
[ As Trump ] Sean, tell your
viewers I'm willing to do it.

00:12:10.167 --> 00:12:12.667
Hold on. The bailiff is
going to take the phone away.

00:12:12.667 --> 00:12:14.767
[ Laughter ]

00:12:14.767 --> 00:12:16.033
[ Normal voice ]
Although the funniest example

00:12:16.033 --> 00:12:18.100
of right-wing pundits
teasing this possibility

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.334
came from Newsmax.

00:12:19.334 --> 00:12:21.834
The anchor tried to be coy
about reporting the news

00:12:21.834 --> 00:12:24.200
that Republicans were floating
Trump as a new speaker,

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.634
but it was not
especially graceful.

00:12:26.634 --> 00:12:27.901
-So far there have been
a few names.

00:12:27.901 --> 00:12:29.601
But remember, it doesn't
necessarily have to be

00:12:29.601 --> 00:12:31.000
a member of Congress, either.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.367
-That is true.
Could be me.

00:12:32.367 --> 00:12:34.133
-It'll be very interesting
to see

00:12:34.133 --> 00:12:35.667
who it could be moving forward.

00:12:35.667 --> 00:12:38.801
-Yeah, no, I think
that's an interesting point.

00:12:38.801 --> 00:12:41.200
I'm glad you brought that up,
that it doesn't have to be

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.367
a member of the House.

00:12:42.367 --> 00:12:44.267
It could be someone else.

00:12:44.267 --> 00:12:46.567
Maybe rhymes with "Trump."
Who knows?

00:12:46.567 --> 00:12:49.133
[ Laughter ]

00:12:49.133 --> 00:12:50.367
-Oh, it rhymes with "Trump"?

00:12:50.367 --> 00:12:53.767
Oh, please tell me
it's one of the Klumps.

00:12:53.767 --> 00:12:55.267
Or all of the Klumps.

00:12:55.267 --> 00:12:56.667
I would love to see
Eddie Murphy

00:12:56.667 --> 00:12:58.534
play every member
of the Republican Party

00:12:58.534 --> 00:13:00.133
at one giant dinner scene.

00:13:00.133 --> 00:13:02.133
I'm guessing it would look
something like this.

00:13:02.133 --> 00:13:04.467
[ Gavel bangs ]
-Hercules. Hercules.

00:13:04.467 --> 00:13:06.667
[ Laughter ]

00:13:08.334 --> 00:13:09.701
-That's enough.

00:13:09.701 --> 00:13:11.767
[ Laughter ]

00:13:11.767 --> 00:13:13.300
House Republicans
don't have a speaker,

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.200
and their standard bearer
is in court for fraud.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.467
You really can't sum up
the current state

00:13:16.467 --> 00:13:17.667
of the party
any better than that.

00:13:17.667 --> 00:13:19.434
In the process,
they've paralyzed Congress.

00:13:19.434 --> 00:13:21.133
Basically, Republicans
pulled down their pants,

00:13:21.133 --> 00:13:23.033
squatted over the Constitution,
and took a giant --

00:13:23.033 --> 00:13:24.334
Well, I won't say it, but it...

00:13:24.334 --> 00:13:25.234
-Rhymes with "Trump."

00:13:25.234 --> 00:13:28.234
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:28.234 --> 00:13:30.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

